    "problemName": "reverse-pairs",
    "language": "python3",
    "code": "class Solution:\r\n    def reversePairs(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\r\n        def merge_sort(l, r):\r\n            if l >= r:\r\n                return 0\r\n            mid = (l + r) >> 1\r\n            ans = merge_sort(l, mid) + merge_sort(mid + 1, r)\r\n            t = []\r\n            i, j = l, mid + 1\r\n            while i <= mid and j <= r:\r\n                if nums[i] <= 2 * nums[j]:\r\n                    i += 1\r\n                else:\r\n                    ans += mid - i + 1\r\n                    j += 1\r\n            i, j = l, mid + 1\r\n            while i <= mid and j <= r:\r\n                if nums[i] <= nums[j]:\r\n                    t.append(nums[i])\r\n                    i += 1\r\n                else:\r\n                    t.append(nums[j])\r\n                    j += 1\r\n            t.extend(nums[i : mid + 1])\r\n            t.extend(nums[j : r + 1])\r\n            nums[l : r + 1] = t\r\n            return ans\r\n\r\n        return merge_sort(0, len(nums) - 1)",
